    "['binding tunnel [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"The equivalent Juniper configuration for the HUAWEI command `binding tunnel gre` would be to bind the GRE tunnel to the physical interface under the GRE tunnel configuration.\\n\\nHere's the translated command:\\n##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n- `gr-0/0/0` represents the GRE tunnel interface (equivalent to Tunnel0 in HUAWEI)\\n- `ge-1/0/0` represents the physical GigabitEthernet interface (equivalent to GigabitEthernet1/0/0 in HUAWEI)\\n- The command links the tunnel's source to the physical interface\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel source ge-1/0/0'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-protocol [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel protocol gre multipoint', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel protocol gre multipoint\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, GRE tunnels are configured under `gr-` interfaces (GRE interfaces)\\n- `unit 0` is used as the logical unit (similar to the interface instance in Huawei)\\n- `tunnel protocol gre multipoint` is Juniper's equivalent to Huawei's `tunnel-protocol gre p2mp` for point-to-multipoint GRE tunnels\\n- The command is placed under the interface hierarchy context in Juniper's configuration style\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 tunnel protocol gre multipoint'}]]": 1,
    "['source [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, GRE interfaces are typically named as `gr-fpc/pic/port` (e.g., gr-0/0/0). The command sets the physical interface (`GigabitEthernet1/0/0` in this case) as the source for the GRE tunnel. The exact GRE interface name may vary based on your Juniper platform and slot configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 tunnel source GigabitEthernet1/0/0'}]]": 1,
    "['ospf network-type [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface Tunnel0 interface-type p2mp', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface Tunnel0 interface-type p2mp\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, OSPF interface network types are configured under the OSPF protocol hierarchy.\\n- The equivalent of Huawei's `ospf network-type p2mp` is setting the interface type to `p2mp` for the specific OSPF area and interface.\\n- The command maintains the same OSPF area (0.0.0.0) and applies the p2mp configuration to the Tunnel0 interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface Tunnel0 interface-type p2mp'}]]": 1,
